> not need to appear in `:ros2_message_types`.

## About

Broadcast a static transform between two frames and look it up from another
node.

Reference implementations (canonical TF2 tutorials):

* C++ static broadcaster — [`geometry2/examples_tf2_cpp/src/static_broadcaster.cpp`](https://github.com/ros2/geometry2/blob/rolling/examples_tf2_cpp/src/static_broadcaster.cpp)
* Python static broadcaster — [`geometry2/examples_tf2_py/examples_tf2_py/static_tf2_broadcaster.py`](https://github.com/ros2/geometry2/blob/rolling/examples_tf2_py/examples_tf2_py/static_tf2_broadcaster.py)
* C++ listener — [`geometry2/examples_tf2_cpp/src/tf2_listener.cpp`](https://github.com/ros2/geometry2/blob/rolling/examples_tf2_cpp/src/tf2_listener.cpp)
* Tutorials — [Writing a tf2 static broadcaster (C++)](https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/Tutorials/Intermediate/Tf2/Writing-A-Tf2-Static-Broadcaster-Cpp.html)
* Background — [`tf2.md`](../tf2.md) in this repo.

Verify from another terminal with:

```sh
ros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo world robot
```

## Generate (only needed if you have other types)

```elixir
Mix.Task.run("rclex.gen", [])
Application.stop(:rclex)
Application.unload(:rclex)
{:ok, _} = Application.ensure_all_started(:rclex)

alias Rclex.Pkgs.Tf2Msgs
alias Rclex.Pkgs.GeometryMsgs
:ok
```

